# Git push and deploy

- **Do not run `git push`** (or equivalent: `gh repo sync`, force-push, etc.) unless the user **explicitly** asks you to push or deploy.
- Local **`git commit`** is fine when it helps the task, but **stop before pushing** so services tied to the remote (e.g. Netlify auto-deploy) do not redeploy on every change.
- When the user wants to ship, they will say so (e.g. “push to origin”, “deploy”, “push it”).
